**Files:** `vibrantix-client-panel/src/components/evidence-management/ControlMappingTable.jsx` — badge renderer
**Root Cause:** The version badge renderer uses a prefix-match that covers only `aws_`, `azure_`, `gcp_`, `k8s_` prefixes. ISO 27001 framework IDs use a different pattern (e.g. `iso27001_2022`). They fall through the match without rendering any version indicator, leaving auditors unable to distinguish the 2013 edition (114 controls) from the current 2022 edition (93 controls).
**Claude Fix Prompt:**
```
File: vibrantix-client-panel/src/components/evidence-management/ControlMappingTable.jsx

In the badge renderer function, add:
  if (frameworkId.includes('iso27001') || frameworkId.includes('27001')) {
    const year = frameworkId.match(/\d{4}/)?.[0];
    if (year >= 2022) return <Badge color="green">ISO 27001:2022</Badge>;
    return <Badge color="yellow">ISO 27001:2013 <Tooltip>Superseded — current standard is 2022</Tooltip></Badge>;
  }
Place this check before the cloud-provider checks to give it priority.
```

**Files:** `vibrantix-client-panel/src/components/evidence-management/ExportShareContent.jsx` — `handleExport`
**Root Cause:** The `handleExport` function wraps all export calls in a generic `catch` that only shows `toast.error('Export failed')`. Unimplemented formats, network timeouts, and server errors all produce the same opaque message. Users cannot distinguish "this format is not yet available" from "something went wrong".
**Claude Fix Prompt:**
```
File: vibrantix-client-panel/src/components/evidence-management/ExportShareContent.jsx

1. For each format button, check implementation status:
   const IMPLEMENTED_FORMATS = ['csv']; // extend as formats are built
   if (!IMPLEMENTED_FORMATS.includes(format)) {
     return <Button disabled tooltip="Coming soon"><Badge>Planned</Badge> {format.toUpperCase()}</Button>;
   }
2. In handleExport error handler, distinguish error types:
   if (err.status === 404) toast.info(`${format} export is not yet available`);
   else if (err.status === 408 || err.status === 504) toast.error('Export timed out — try a smaller date range');
   else toast.error(`Export failed: ${err.message}`);
3. Add a progress indicator while export is in-flight.
```
